From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:04:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shader_split: spill each scan result to disk instead of
 pickling the batch back

A batch's results come back through the pool's result queue, which
pickles the whole batch into one bytes object. One file holding
thousands of shaders is too large for that copy and dies with
MemoryError in _sendback_result, after every file has already been
scanned: Hyrule Warriors: Age of Imprisonment reaches progress
2153/2153 with 9,766 shaders and then fails, and chunk=1 does not
help because a single file's result alone is too large to pickle.

Workers now pickle each scan result to a spill directory beside the
map as it is scanned and send back only its path, so the queue
carries small strings. pooled() is a generator yielding results in
job order, loading each spilled result and removing its file, and
main() merges each result into the shader tables as it arrives
instead of holding every file's result until the scan ends, so the
parent keeps only the deduplicated keys. A spill failure falls back
to the in-memory result for that job, and no spill directory falls
back to the old behaviour entirely. The spill directory is removed
once the scan ends, including on red().

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: one file's scan result is too large for the pool's result queue to pickle, so the split dies with MemoryError after scanning everything
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#123

